Z||000000||AusFiero||08-18-2001||12:50 AM||||Well I didn't want to show any of this until it was all finished and I had a nice set of complete panels sitting together on the floor, but seeing I was asked here is a picture of one of the plugs to be used to make a mould off in its almost finished form. One of the original mounts is still filled in this picture and the tabs to hold the skirts up will be aluminum for moulding reasons. 1 mount that used to hold the aero trim on is no longer needed. A new one is on the lower edge of the panel.<BR>This plug is ready for final sanding and is getting sanded, primed and painted today then polished to a glass finish tomorrow ready for moulding off. The other side is almost finished also. I reshaped the bottom of the scooops 3 times to get them right. They could have passed but I am fussy. The door and front guard pieces are almost ready for some more sanding work soon and they too will be painted black to check for straightness etc then buffed and polished before being moulded off. This is the one and only picture I am going to show now though until I have a complete set to photgraph just before they get shipped this coming week.<BR>ooops...crappy and large pic, was a gif, try this JPG<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sidescoop001.jpg"> <P>For those that seen my wife fell ill in the other post, no I am not at the hospital yet. Seems she is feeling better and is undergoing more tests. Not a place to take a 3 and 5 year old until later. They would run amok. Well they are here too but at least I can lock the garage door   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 08-18-2001).]||202.139.20.3||reg||3
